<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aristides</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 530–468 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Aristides the Just</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aristides, called the Just, was an Athenian statesman and general. He fought at Marathon in 490 BCE, was ostracised in 482 after opposing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistocles">Themistocles</a>, and was recalled to command at Salamis and Plataea in 480–479. In 478–477 he assessed the contributions of ships or money owed by the members of the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a>, and his fairness gave him his lasting nickname.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aristides.jpg" alt="Aristides" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Another Believer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boston_(2019)_-_194.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Athenian <b>Aristides</b> assessed each member's contribution of ships or money, set at 460 talents a year.</blockquote><a href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Alopeke, in what is now <a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>. Died in Classical Athens, in what is now <a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=37.95,23.75&amp;year=-490" aria-label="Alopeke on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5142 799 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Aristides"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5592 1069h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5592 1069h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=37.95,23.75&amp;year=-490">What was here in 490 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
